- op: discuss  # bc85
  at: '2026-06-03T00:12:28Z'  # bc85
  by: agent  # bc85
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bc85
  clock: 5  # bc85
  nonce: bc85  # bc85
  message: "Pass-40 F40.B1+B3+B4 batch — 6 read-subcommands × 5 input shapes matrix (18/30 unhandled traceback cells).\n\nMatrix: search, slice, explain, dead-code-maybe, symbols, routes × {missing-file, empty-file (1 byte newline), wrong-schema ({foo:bar}), array-root ([1,2,3]), null-nodes ({schema_version:..., nodes:null})}.\n\nF40.B1 (HEADLINE): empty behavior_map.get('nodes', []) fallback masks input-shape errors. For input {foo:bar}, every read-subcommand calls behavior_map.get('nodes', []) which returns [] because {foo:bar} IS a dict (just no 'nodes' key). Subcommand iterates empty list, produces rc=0 with 'No X found'. Conflates two distinct conditions: (a) 'valid behavior map with no matches' and (b) 'input is not a behavior map at all'. 4 of 6 subcommands exit rc=0 in case (b): search, dead-code-maybe, symbols, routes. Only slice and explain return rc=1 (because their --entry positional fails to find a match; the input-shape problem stays invisible).\n\nF40.B3: empty file (1 byte newline) tracebacks 6/6 at json.decoder. For a file containing only '\\n', json.load raises JSONDecodeError: 'Expecting value: line 2 column 1' and all 6 subcommands propagate. Sibling failure mode to F40.B1 — same boundary, different shape.\n\nF40.B4: symbols/routes emit cache-status footer 'Using 1 cached / [cached] /tmp/p40_wrong_schema.json / Output: stdout' even on wrong-schema input. The 'Using 1 cached' line treats the input file as a cached behavior map; there's no schema check at the cache-resolver layer either. Distinct boundary from F40.B1 — a SECOND instance of trust-input-shape assumption.\n\nCell-by-cell:\n|   | missing | empty | wrong_schema | array | null_nodes |\n| search | clean | tb | rc=0 'No symbols' | tb | tb |\n| slice | clean | tb | rc=1 'No symbol main' | tb | tb |\n| explain | clean | tb | rc=1 'No symbol main' | tb | tb |\n| dead-code-maybe | clean | tb | rc=0 'No prod fns' | tb | tb |\n| symbols | clean | tb | rc=0 cached/empty | tb | tb |\n| routes | clean | tb | rc=0 cached/empty | tb | tb |\n18/30 (60%) unhandled traceback cells. 6/6 traceback on empty, array, null_nodes; 0/6 on missing-file (the only consistent shape-handler); 0/6 on wrong_schema (false-clean rc=0).\n\nF40.B2 contrast: missing-file is the ONLY uniformly-handled shape — 6/6 produce identical 'Error: Input file not found: /path' with rc=1 and zero tracebacks. A clean handler exists but is path-only; doesn't extend to content-validation. Suggests the input-shape validation should be hoisted into the same _open_or_die helper.\n\nFix path: schema-validate at the load boundary; reject inputs lacking schema_version/nodes before fan-out. Cache-resolver layer needs same check (F40.B4)."  # bc85
